# Binary Tree Postorder Traversal (Recursive)

## Problem

Return the postorder traversal of a binary tree.

Traversal Order

Left

↓

Right

↓

Root

----------------------------------------

## Algorithm

1. If root is NULL, return.
2. Traverse the left subtree.
3. Traverse the right subtree.
4. Visit the current node.

----------------------------------------

## Dry Run

Tree

        1
      /   \
     2     3
    / \   / \
   4   5 6   7

Traversal

4 → 5 → 2 → 6 → 7 → 3 → 1

Output

4 5 2 6 7 3 1

----------------------------------------

## Time Complexity

O(n)

Every node is visited once.

----------------------------------------

## Space Complexity

O(h)

h = Height of the tree

Worst Case : O(n)

Balanced Tree : O(log n)

----------------------------------------

## Pattern

postorder(left);

postorder(right);

Visit Root;

----------------------------------------

## Important Points

✅ Base Case

```cpp
if(root == NULL)
    return;
```

✅ Pass vector by reference

```cpp
vector<int>& ans
```

No extra copy is created.

✅ Postorder means

Left

↓

Right

↓

Root

----------------------------------------

## Traversal Difference

Preorder

Root → Left → Right

Inorder

Left → Root → Right

Postorder

Left → Right → Root